    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0019" n="7" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.840 Welles, Sumner/25: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-02-13T12:00:00+01:00">February 13,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 13—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. Department’s 32, February 12, 1 p.m. For Welles. I conveyed to Count Ciano
                    this morning your appreciation of his message and he assured me that he and the
                    Chief of the Government will be glad to receive you immediately after your
                    arrival, presumably on the 26th.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
